    {
      "slug": "maximilian-ii-his-wife-and-three-children-q27981200",
      "title": "Maximilian II, His Wife and Three Children",
      "year": 1563,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/Giuseppe_Arcimboldi_003.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 1432,
      "imageHeight": 1798,
      "story": "Depicted alongside Maximilian II, Holy Roman Emperor are his consort, Maria of Austria, Holy Roman Empress, and their eldest daughter, Anna of Austria, Queen of Spain (born 1549); behind them is Rudolf (born 1552) and, in the cradle, Ernst (born 1553). Their clothing is in keeping with Spanish fashions at mid-century. The kings doublet and shoes have long vents, while the short trousers illustrate the characteristic combination of a smooth base fabric to which strips made of the same material as the doublet have been attached. The clothing of the queen and of Archduchess Anna features a form of skirt that is already stiff but not yet very wide.",
